3. No sale or paid access

You must not sell, rent, lease, or otherwise provide the Software in exchange
for money or other consideration. This prohibition applies to the original
Software, modified versions, and covered portions, whether distributed alone,
embedded in another product, or included in a paid bundle.

In particular, you must not charge for copies, downloads, distribution,
licenses, activation, subscriptions, or hosted access to the Software or its
functionality. Calling a required payment a donation, membership, handling
fee, hosting fee, or support fee does not avoid this prohibition. No time
limit or later conversion to a license allowing sale is provided by this
license.

Genuinely voluntary donations are permitted if payment is not a condition of
obtaining, using, or accessing the Software or any covered functionality.
You may charge for independent services such as support, training, or
consulting, provided the Software remains available without payment and the
service is neither a required purchase nor a disguised charge for the
Software or access to it.

4. Conditions for sharing and modifications

The Software remains subject to this license when you use, copy, modify, or
incorporate it into another program. Creating a modification, changing its
name, or incorporating covered code into a larger work does not remove this
license or the attribution requirements. This applies to each subsequent
modified version and redistribution. Mere use as a tool does not make your
independent work a derivative of the Software; see section 5.

Whenever you distribute the Software or make a hosted version available:

a. Provide a complete copy of this license and retain the applicable
   copyright, attribution, and license notices, including the accompanying
   NOTICE file. Identify Filterstudio and its original author, drlechk, and
   contributors, and include the original project URL:
   https://github.com/drlechk/filterstudio
   In a modified or combined work, clearly identify the Filterstudio code
   as the source of the reused material. A suitable attribution is:
   "Based on Filterstudio by drlechk and contributors -
   https://github.com/drlechk/filterstudio".
   For an interactive application or hosted version, make this credit,
   the copyright notices, and the license readily accessible in the user
   interface, such as a Credits or About page. For other distributions,
   provide them in the accompanying documentation. Retain these notices
   in private copies as well; private use alone does not require a public
   acknowledgement or publication of private modifications.
b. Make modified versions and covered portions available under this same
   license. Do not remove the no-sale condition or offer the covered material
   under terms that permit its sale or paid access. Independent materials
   that do not incorporate or derive from the Software are not subject to
   this requirement.
c. Clearly identify substantial modifications and do not imply that the
   original authors endorse your version.

Recipients receive permission directly from the respective Licensors under
this license. You may not impose additional terms or technical restrictions
that prevent recipients from exercising the rights granted here. Private
